  "learn": {
    "title": "Guarded Servo",
    "body": "Wire the servo signal to D9, VCC to 5V and GND to GND. Wire the pot end1 to 5V, end2 to GND and wiper to A0. Connect the button between D2 and GND with INPUT_PULLUP.\n\nWith the button released, park at 90°. While held, map A0 from 0–1023 to 0–180°, then constrain travel to 30–150°. The enable condition takes priority over the knob: releasing must park immediately. Print PARK on release.\n\nRun, hold the button and move the knob to 0%, then 100%, then release. Observe 30°, 150°, then 90° in the servo inspector. The simulator models commanded angle, not load, stall current or mechanical collision; a physical servo needs a suitable supply and common ground.",
    "links": []
  },
